From: Hannes Janetzek <hannes.janetzek@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:59:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA mixer: skip controls the mixer list can't match before
 opening them

Each alsaaudio.Mixer() opens the card and loads all of its elements, and
get_mixer_zctrls() opened about three per control before checking the
symbol against SOUNDCARD_MIXER. On a card with many controls this is
quadratic: the Pixel 3's SDM845 codec has 1178 controls (~21 ms per open),
so zynthian spent ~74 s in it at startup, and with an empty SOUNDCARD_MIXER
it kept none of them. Controls whose name no listed symbol can stand for are
now dropped first: startup on the Pixel 3 goes from ~76 s to 8 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 70497ea3c49d83cc44920546fafac6d430226c66)
---
 zyngine/zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer.py | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/zyngine/zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer.py b/zyngine/zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer.py
index 84647c34..faa27edb 100644
--- a/zyngine/zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer.py
+++ b/zyngine/zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer.py
@@ -221,6 +221,15 @@ class zynthian_engine_alsa_mixer(zynthian_engine):
         try:
             is_log = False
             mixer_ctrl_names = sorted(set(alsaaudio.mixers(device=device)))
+            if ctrl_list:
+                # Each alsaaudio.Mixer() opens the card and loads all its elements: skip the
+                # controls no symbol in the list can stand for before opening them (phone
+                # codecs have >1000 routing controls: minutes at startup otherwise)
+                wanted = set(ctrl_list)
+                def is_wanted(ctrl_name):
+                    base = ctrl_name.replace(' ', '_')
+                    return any(s == base or s.startswith(base + "_") for s in wanted)
+                mixer_ctrl_names = [c for c in mixer_ctrl_names if is_wanted(c)]
             for ctrl_name in mixer_ctrl_names:
                 idx = 0  # ALSA array index
                 try:
